From 9b30d16ee08869c6e2be70a4bff670f6f8e6c225 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:36:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Classic and Horizon medals: four new medals, a scrolling
 medal view with drawn medals, gold edges on what Horizon adds

The medal table holds 20 rows and knows three more conditions: every card in a range, every species a partner can
be, and the city's residents (the original ones or all of them). A row can ask for an option and can hide its medal
without it; hidden medals are not counted on the Player page.

The medal view shows a grid of five medals a row that scrolls by rows, a large picture of the selected medal, its
name, two lines of text and a state line: earned, a count, or not earned yet. The pictures come from the species
file (content/medals) and are loaded over the old coin stamps when the view opens; the spinning coin and its mesh
buffer are gone.

Chart, City page and card album draw a gold edge on the boxes of what the original game did not have.
